{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Final report — /rebar-debug Phase 2 landed for review (Option A)\n\n**Gerrit change:** https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2365 (commit `902f027a3d5c`,\n`rebar-ticket:` trailer + DCO). Plan-review **PASS / certified** at head `902f027a`\n(`verified_at_sha` 483477df, currency_basis file_impact). Awaiting `LLM-Review +1` + `Verified +1`\nbefore Submit; ticket stays `in_progress` until merged.\n\n**Problem.** `_reads._tracker` gated reads on `os.path.isdir(tracker)` only, so a directory that\nexists but is not a usable store returned `[]` instead of raising `store_uninitialized` — a broken\nstore indistinguishable from an empty one.\n\n**Proven root cause (RCA in prior comment).** `_reads._tracker()` (`src/rebar/_reads.py`) fires the\nguard only when the dir is ABSENT; a present-but-unusable tracker (marker files, no `.git`, or\n`.git` with unresolvable HEAD) satisfies `isdir`, so every library/MCP read reduced to `[]`.\nAttributed to `44fd-230c-5893-4246` (commit `84fc5f9b`).\n\n**Final predicate (operator-approved Option A — one shared content-based seam).**\n`store_usability.store_is_usable(tracker)` = `isdir` AND EITHER\n1. `.git` present AND `git rev-parse --verify -q HEAD` resolves (via the store's bounded runner), OR\n2. carries store STRUCTURE — a committed `.store-compat.json` record, OR ≥1 non-dot event dir\n   (legacy fallback, mirrors `reducer/_api.py`).\n\nBoth `_reads._tracker` and the write guard `event_prepare._ensure_initialized` call this ONE\npredicate — no mode flag, no second path — so read and write cannot diverge.\n\n**Three-case matrix (all test-pinned, GREEN):**\n| Case | Fixtures | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| Production incident — marker files only, no `.git`/`.store-compat.json`/event dirs | `_tracker_present_without_git` | **RAISES `store_uninitialized`** ✅ |\n| Empty-but-initialized LIVE store — `.git` + resolvable HEAD | `_initialized_empty_repo` | reads `[]` ✅ |\n| Materialized snapshot — `.git`-LESS, committed `.store-compat.json` + event dir | `_gitless_snapshot_repo` | **READS** ✅ (gate-agent regression fix) |\n\n**Empty-snapshot edge (operator ruling):** a `.git`-less snapshot with `.store-compat.json` and\nZERO events is VALID via the committed marker → reads `[]`\n(`test_empty_materialized_snapshot_reads_empty`). The predicate is never keyed on emptiness.\n\n**Write-path timeout fix.** The HEAD probe reuses `gitutil.run_git_bounded(tracker, \"rev-parse\",\n\"--verify\", \"-q\", \"HEAD\", timeout=...)` — the store's existing bounded runner (folds\n`TimeoutExpired`→rc 124; `OSError` propagates). No unbounded git call enters the write path;\n`test_store_write_git_timeout_c2ba::test_stage_and_commit_git_calls_are_all_timeout_bounded` GREEN.\n\n**Test (RED→GREEN, held out from the fix, mutation-checked).**\n`tests/unit/test_reads_uninitialized_store.py`. New: `test_materialized_snapshot_reads_instead_of_raising`,\n`test_empty_materialized_snapshot_reads_empty`, and the seeded-mutation guard\n`test_store_structure_clause_is_load_bearing_for_snapshot_reads` (strip clause 2 → snapshot read\nreturns to RAISE), plus the extended `store_is_usable` predicate matrix. Mutation seam exercised via\n`monkeypatch` of `_carries_store_structure`.\n\n**Caller-sweep re-verification (against the NEW predicate).** Broad run\n`pytest tests/unit tests/interfaces -n auto` = **16419 passed**. The 6 previously-red tests are now\nGREEN: `test_gate_ticket_snapshot` ×4, `test_next_batch_compute::test_library_and_mcp_shape`,\n`test_store_write_git_timeout_c2ba`. All 7 `_tracker` entry points + the `.git`-less snapshot path\nbehave correctly; the sole `store_uninitialized` consumer (`audit.server._audited_tickets`)\ndegrades safely and now logs.\n\n**Scope & safety.** Restores read/write parity (no new capability, no new dependency); no existing\ntest weakened (only `test_reads_uninitialized_store.py` touched among tests). `make lint`\n(complexity ratchet new=0/increased=0) + `make typecheck` PASS.\n\n**Pre-existing environmental failures (NOT mine, do not fix).** 8 sandbox-git topology failures —\n`test_atomic_completion_close.py` ×5, `test_rebar_repo_isolation.py::test_copy_repoints_sibling_origin_and_keeps_refs_isolated`,\n`test_tracker_footprint_cli.py` ×2 — all fail with `git … show-ref/ls-tree refs/heads/tickets`\n→ exit 128 on clean `origin/main`; none is in this diff. Separately, one load-only flake surfaced\nunder `-n auto` (`test_wiki_render_hardening.py::test_a_timeout_reaps_the_whole_process_group_not_just_the_child`)\nbut passes 3/3 in isolation and is unrelated to store usability.\n\n**Siblings (Step 7 parity).** CLI read path (`reads_cli.py`) and other bare-`isdir` read sites →\n`free-slothful-fennecfox` (be80-8377-4b4c-44f4), `discovered_from` this ticket.\n\n**Replication.** The original report (a present-but-unusable tracker read returning `[]`) no longer\nreproduces: `rebar.list_tickets` on a marker-file-only dir now raises `store_uninitialized`\n(production-incident AC, GREEN).\n\nClose will carry `--class=plan_defect --caused-by=44fd-230c-5893-4246` once the change is\n`Verified +1` and merged."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787970115688778001,"uuid":"27f8a2e7-6133-4d64-9927-fdc0a0f94f28"}